### 8. MOVIE
### Depends on nothing directly; relations added afterward.
### ============================================================

### 8.1 Create Movie
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "HTTP Test Movie {{$timestamp}}",
  "originalTitle": "HTTP Test Movie",
  "synopsis": "Movie created from IntelliJ HTTP Client.",
  "director": "Test Director",
  "language": "English",
  "subtitle": "Vietnamese",
  "ageRating": "T13",
  "durationMinutes": 150,
  "releaseDate": "2030-01-01",
  "endDate": "2030-12-31",
  "showingStatus": "NOW_SHOWING",
  "posterUrl": "https://example.com/poster.jpg",
  "backdropUrl": "https://example.com/backdrop.jpg",
  "trailerYoutubeUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=test",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

> {%
client.global.set("movieId", String(response.body["data"]["id"]));
%}


### 8.2 Get Movie by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/{{movieId}}
Accept: application/json


### 8.3 Get all / filter Movies
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies?showingStatus=NOW_SHOWING&status=ACTIVE&language=English&page={{page}}&size={{size}}
Accept: application/json


